{"title":"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Four of the angle measurements <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/f/77f99c1836fcf07b4f98fd1bf851401b057bfb01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$62^{\\circ}, 85^{\\circ}, 99^{\\circ}, 108^{\\circ}, 114^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" /> are the measures of the angles in the same quadrilateral. Which angle measure is not?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/8/538606c265d5ffcb9bdafbca15870722f06afea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 62^{\\circ} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 85^{\\circ} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 99^{\\circ} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 108^{\\circ} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 114^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"453\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of the angles in a quadrilateral is always <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/b/96bd59024f5cb49b070ca9b0f8906499940c75e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360^{\\circ}$\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />, so we can find the sum of all of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> angles listed and then subtract that from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/b/96bd59024f5cb49b070ca9b0f8906499940c75e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360^{\\circ}$\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> to see which one is <i>not</i> an angle of the quadrilateral:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/4/44443923c25b03ff469a50bbddf313d208cb90a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$62^{\\circ} + 85^{\\circ} + 99^{\\circ} + 108^{\\circ} + 114^{\\circ} = 147^{\\circ} + 207^{\\circ} + 114^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"411\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/8/098ea481f1c46fafc45454b6c948b6bddef22c6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=354^{\\circ} + 114^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/b/acbf337d956d018578901ddbc92ea7758db3954d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=468^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>The angle that is <i>not</i> in the quadrilateral is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/3/bd3188b743c0d456a57cb20b6427b7b3b0f7ea1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$468^{\\circ} - 360^{\\circ} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 108^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"200\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Gra